shuvscode: first-class multiplexer support on terminal reattach (v2).

When the persistent-terminal patch (28) keeps a pty alive across a same-window
project switch or reload, VS Code's replay mechanism serializes the xterm cell
buffer on the pty host and writes those bytes back into a fresh xterm in the
renderer. That works for "shell at a prompt" terminals but corrupts the UI of
any program living on the alternate screen buffer: zellij, tmux, neovim, btop,
lazygit, etc. The stale snapshot is painted, the running multiplexer is unaware
its client changed and therefore doesn't redraw, and any subsequent output
lands on top of the stale frame.

This patch teaches the replay path to detect alternate-buffer terminals and,
after the renderer has settled into its real layout size, force a real
SIGWINCH on the pty so the inner foreground process group redraws itself from
authoritative state. The renderer still runs its normal replay (which is what
restores xterm modes such as mouse reporting, focus events, and bracketed
paste) so click handling, scrolling, etc. continue to work.

Mechanics:

  1. Pty host (`XtermSerializer`): tag the replay event with `altBufferActive`
     by checking `_xterm.buffer.active.type === 'alternate'` at serialize
     time, and expose a `getCurrentDimensions()` helper that returns the
     serializer xterm's live cols/rows.

  2. Pty host (`PersistentTerminalProcess.triggerReplay`): after firing the
     replay event, if `altBufferActive` is true, schedule a delayed SIGWINCH
     bump (250ms + 50ms restore). At fire time we read the current cols/rows
     from the serializer (which the renderer has updated via its post-attach
     `resize()` call), so we don't use the stale recorded background size and
     squish the multiplexer into a narrow column count.

  3. The replay event interface gains an optional `altBufferActive` flag so
     older backends and event consumers keep working unchanged.

The renderer (`BasePty.handleReplay`) is intentionally unchanged: the normal
replay restores xterm mode state (mouse reporting, focus events, bracketed
paste), and the stale cell paint into the alt buffer is harmless because the
delayed SIGWINCH triggers a full redraw by the multiplexer moments later.

